    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "They can act like patient tutors, offering explanations in many voices, adapting to confusion, not judgment. They can generate practice problems, visualize ideas, or translate symbols into stories. But they shouldn't replace thinking — they should spark it. Like a compass, not a map."
